   "claims": [
    {
     "id": "financial_health.0",
     "text": "Revenue grew from $12.78bn (FY2020) to $19.28bn (FY2025), an 8.6% compound rate, but only 3.9% in the most recent year — the growth curve has flattened, not reversed.",
     "source_ids": [
      "s1"
     ],
     "confidence": "high",
     "as_of": "2025-03-31"
    },
    {
     "id": "financial_health.1",
     "text": "Operating income rose to $4.07bn while net income was flat at $3.16bn: margins are being defended even as growth slows.",
     "source_ids": [
      "s1"
     ],
     "confidence": "high",
     "as_of": "2025-03-31"
    },
    {
     "id": "financial_health.2",
     "text": "Cash and equivalents nearly doubled to $2.86bn over two years, and the exchange reports return on equity of 36.7% with an operating margin of 27.1% — this is a cash-generative business, not one under funding pressure.",
     "source_ids": [
      "s1",
      "s2"
     ],
     "confidence": "high",
     "as_of": "2026-08-27"
    },
    {
     "id": "financial_health.3",
     "text": "R&D spend is $153m against $19.3bn of revenue (0.8%), which is characteristic of a services business: the money follows billable delivery, not product engineering.",
     "source_ids": [
      "s1"
     ],
     "confidence": "high",
     "as_of": "2025-03-31"
    },
    {
     "id": "financial_health.4",
     "text": "The 20-F risk factors put client concentration and fixed-price delivery first: 'Our failure to complete fixed-price and fixed-timeframe contracts within budget and on time may negatively affect our profitability', and 'Our client contracts are often conditional upon our performance'.",
